- CompilerOptions.Effect (`*etscore.EffectPluginOptions`): `CompilerOptions::effect: EffectOptionsCell`, an
  `RwLock<Option<Arc<ets_etscore::EffectPluginOptions>>>` with `get`/`set`. tsrs_core depends on the workspace's
  ets_etscore crate (a leaf crate with no tsrs dependency), as Go's core imports etscore, so the field holds the
  concrete type and there is no crate cycle.
- tsrs-only: the cell. Go assigns `program.Options().Effect` after the program is built (etsdiagnostics'
  `--effect-config` override), and tsrs shares a program's options immutably (`P<CompilerOptions>`), so the field
  takes that write through a shared reference.
- Clone: `EffectOptionsCell::clone` copies the current `Arc` into a new cell (Go's shallow copy of the pointer).
- Equals (`reflect.DeepEqual(options.Effect, other.Effect)`): `PartialEq` compares the options by value.
- core/effect_options_test.go: src/effect_options_test.rs (plus a Rust-only test of the shared assignment).

